The solution over-corrects. An integer divisible by all three of 4, 6, 10 is a multiple of 60, and it lies in **all three** pairwise categories, not exactly one. The pairwise sets have sizes 41, 25, 16 (sum 82). Elements in exactly one pair contribute once; multiples of 60 (there are 8) are counted three times and must be counted once — but the solution subtracts 8 from each category, dropping them entirely (counted 3 − 3 = 0 times).

Correct count: 82 − 2·8 = 66. (E.g., inclusion–exclusion: 41+25+16 − 8−8−8 + 8 = 66.)

